  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Consider the graph of $y=x^3+4x^2-3x-18$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A positive-leading cubic touching the $x$-axis at $(-3,0)$, crossing it at $(2,0)$ and passing through $(0,-18)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3+4x^2-3x-18&=(x+3)(x^2+x-6)\\\\x^3+4x^2-3x-18&=(x+3)^2(x-2).\\end{align*}$$\nThe double root $x=-3$ gives a touch at $(-3,0)$; the simple root $x=2$ gives a crossing at $(2,0)$. The $y$-intercept is $(0,-18)$. The positive leading term gives a curve descending to the left and rising to the right.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p33-q8-a-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 33 question 8(a); teacher page 63 Section K 8(a)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.08cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-4.8,-27) rectangle (3.4,29);\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt,black] (-4.6,0)--(3.1,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt,black] (0,-25)--(0,26) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt,domain=-4.5:2.75,samples=160] plot (\\x,{(\\x+3)^2*(\\x-2)});\n\\node[above] at (-3,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$-3$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\node[below right] at (2,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$2$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 60,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 33,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 8(a); answer figure in teacher PDF page 63, printed page 392, Section K",
                "description": "Equation-driven cubic sketch with arrowed axes, labelled roots −3 and 2, no grid and no origin label. Ordinary curve and axes use house black.",
                "mathematics": "y=(x+3)^2(x-2); double root −3, simple root 2, y-intercept −18. The curve touches at −3 and crosses at 2.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only; no graph or grid is supplied in the student question."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 75
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A horizontal line $y=h$ intersects the graph at $(x_1,y_1)$, $(x_2,y_2)$ and $(x_3,y_3)$. Show that the average $$\\frac{x_1+x_2+x_3}{3}$$ does not depend upon the value of $h$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{4}{3}$.\n\nVieta’s formula gives $x_1+x_2+x_3=-4$, independently of $h$.",
          "worked": "At the intersections,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3+4x^2-3x-18&=h\\\\x^3+4x^2-3x-(18+h)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBy Vieta’s formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}x_1+x_2+x_3&=-\\frac{4}{1}\\\\x_1+x_2+x_3&=-4\\\\\\frac{x_1+x_2+x_3}{3}&=-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe average does not depend upon $h$, since changing $h$ changes only the constant coefficient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
